From efcb1f525525d9c4ce947266c577bac35fafd837 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:45:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): GIL-safe SIGUSR2 stack dump instead of
 faulthandler.register [daveey]

faulthandler.register(SIGUSR2, all_threads=True) dumps from C signal context on
whichever thread caught the signal and walks every other thread's frame chain
while those threads run, without the GIL. A thread popping a frame mid-walk
makes dump_frame read freed memory: David-MBP gateway 43117 segfaulted in
faulthandler_user -> _Py_DumpTracebackThreads -> dump_frame ->
_PyFrame_SafeGetCode on 10-30, losing 4 in-flight Kanban runs.

SIGUSR2 now installs a Python-level signal.signal handler (ThreadStackDumper,
gateway/sigusr2_stack_dump.py) that runs on the main thread with the GIL held,
snapshots sys._current_frames(), names threads from threading.enumerate(), and
appends a timestamped dump to the same gateway_faulthandler.log via a raw fd
write. A second SIGUSR2 within 1 s of the last dump is ignored; a write error
is swallowed so SIGUSR2 never terminates the gateway. faulthandler.enable() for
fatal errors is unchanged; Windows (no SIGUSR2) is unchanged.
---
